We now set (or refresh) the secret token used for `ochami` commands. Stop here
if no token came back (for example because the request to the token service
was sent through a proxy); every `ochami` call below would otherwise fail
later, less clearly.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Set Access token -->
```bash
CLUSTER_ACCESS_TOKEN=$(gen_access_token)
if [[ -z "${CLUSTER_ACCESS_TOKEN}" ]]; then
	echo "ERROR: gen_access_token returned an empty token" >&2
	exit 1
fi
export CLUSTER_ACCESS_TOKEN
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
